[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   TEP-9 step 061 -- aphelion-sky channel: tide calibration and the
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   m=1 dipole
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   The transit analyses (steps 030-060) test the RECONSTRUCTION channel:
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   how badly a standard-dynamics clock describes the inbound trajectory.
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   This step tests the complementary SPATIAL channel on the same comets:
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   where their original-orbit aphelia actually point on the sky.
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   Two measurements, both strictly real-data:
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   T1  galactic-tide calibration.  The dominant known anisotropy of
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   Oort-spike aphelia is the galactic tide, which is axisymmetric
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   about the galactic pole and concentrates aphelia toward the
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   galactic plane.  The pipeline's directional machinery must
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   recover that known structure to be trusted on the unknown one.
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   Test: distribution of |b_gal| of the aphelia vs isotropic
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   (two-sample KS against a uniform-sphere draw, and the
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   mean |b_gal|).
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   T2  the m=1 dipole toward the boundary axis.  A tide cannot
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   produce an m=1 asymmetry along a fixed ecliptic direction --
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   it is axisymmetric about the galactic pole.  The measured
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   dipole component along the pre-declared axis is therefore a
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   clean observable:
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   d_par = < aph_i . axis >
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   calibrated against a TIDE-AWARE Monte-Carlo null that resamples
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   galactic longitudes uniform while retaining the observed
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   |b_gal| distribution (random hemisphere sign).  This is the
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   spatial analogue of the clock-channel test: does the sky
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   itself lean toward the axis?
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   Samples: Warsaw spike (orig aphelia, 0<1/a<100e-6), CODE class-1
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   matched, and the lpc one-apparition cohort -- three increasingly
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   independent draws of the same population.
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   Axes: both TNO axes plus the antipode and galactic-pole control.
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   Outputs: results/step_b26_aphelion_dipole.json,
[2026-09-21 14:37:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 061]   figures/supplementary/step_b26_aphelion_dipole.png
